constructors
---------------
What is a constructor?
→ In JavaScript, the constructor() method is a special function inside a class.Whenever you create an object using the ‘new’ keyword, JavaScript automatically calls the constructor.
→ Its job is to set initial values for the object’s properties.”
note: constructor is used to initialize instance variables of the class.


this keyword
-------------
--> this is a keyword and a reference variable which holds the reference
    of current class object and points to current class object.

--> this keyword is used to access current class object and the members 
    of the current class.

uses of this keyword :
--------------------
1. this keyword is used to access current class variables.

   syntax: this.instanceVariableName;

2. this keyword is used to access current class methods.

   syntax: this.instanceMethodName();
